  "result": "The root cause is in `split_arg_string` at `src/click/shell_completion.py:603`, and I've written the plan to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-breezy-lollipop.md`. I haven't edited any code because plan mode is active.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` uses `shlex.shlex(string, posix=True)`, and `shlex` treats `#` as a comment character by default. Everything from the first `#` onward is silently dropped, so `prog a#b ` is parsed as `[\"prog\", \"a\"]` and the completion context is wrong.\n\n**Plan:**\n1. In `split_arg_string`, set `lex.commenters = \"\"` after `lex.whitespace_split = True`. The shell has already handled real comments before the line reaches Click.\n2. Add test cases to `tests/test_shell_completion.py` for `example a#b c` -> `[\"example\", \"a#b\", \"c\"]` and for the incomplete-quote form `example 'a#b` -> `[\"example\", \"a#b\"]`.\n3. Add a bugfix entry to `CHANGES.md`.\n4. Run `pytest tests/test_shell_completion.py` to verify.\n\n`ExitPlanMode` isn't available in this session, so approval can't go through the usual prompt. Tell me to proceed and I'll implement it.",
